content:
The datasheet defines one product (OP27GI4-02D, 800G OSFP FR4) with four CWDM lanes in the wavelength assignment table (λ0–λ3). Min/max wavelengths co-occur only on those rows. Application text lists 800G Ethernet, FR4, and IEEE 802.3dj together for that module—not as separate selectable modes—so each lane mode uses `"FR4"` as the application tied to the optical spec table.

```json
{
  "modes": [
    {
      "label": "FR4 CWDM λ0",
      "wavelength_min_nm": 1264.5,
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1277.5,
      "standards_code": "FR4"
    },
    {
      "label": "FR4 CWDM λ1",
      "wavelength_min_nm": 1284.5,
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1297.5,
      "standards_code": "FR4"
    },
    {
      "label": "FR4 CWDM λ2",
      "wavelength_min_nm": 1304.5,
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1317.5,
      "standards_code": "FR4"
    },
    {
      "label": "FR4 CWDM λ3",
      "wavelength_min_nm": 1324.5,
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1337.5,
      "standards_code": "FR4"
    }
  ]
}
```
